.TH PMV 1 "2026-07-02" "PMV" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pmv \- OpenBSD process mitigation viewer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pmv
[\fB--help\fR|\fB-h\fR]
[\fB--version\fR]
[\fB--quiet\fR|\fB-q\fR]
[\fB--pid\fR \fIPID\fR]
[\fB--format\fR \fIjson\fR|\fIcsv\fR]
[\fB--diff\fR]
[\fB--scan-wx\fR \fIPID\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
PMV displays per-process security mitigation status on OpenBSD.
It reads kernel process information via the kvm(3) interface
and shows pledge(2), unveil(2), W^X, and chroot status for each
running process.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \--help, \-h
Display this help message and exit.
.TP
.B \--version
Display version information and exit.
.TP
.B \--quiet, \-q
Suppress table output; useful with \fB--format\fR for scripted exports.
.TP
.B \--pid \fIPID\fR
Filter results to show only the given PID and its children.
.TP
.B \--format \fIjson\fR|\fIcsv\fR
Export process data in structured format.
Writes to stdout, or to output.json/output.csv when combined with \fB--quiet\fR.
.TP
.B \--diff
Compare current process state against the last saved snapshot.
.TP
.B \--scan-wx \fIPID\fR
Scan memory regions of the given PID for W^X violations.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I .pmv_snapshot
Internal snapshot file for diff tracking (auto-generated).
.TP
.I output.json
JSON export file (when used with \fB--quiet --format json\fR).
.TP
.I output.csv
CSV export file (when used with \fB--quiet --format csv\fR).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
on success, 1 on error.
.SH AUTHOR
Jefferson Cesar Antunes
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kvm (3),
.BR pledge (2),
.BR unveil (2)
